maithila, a. relating to Mithilā;
 m. 🞄king of Mithilā;
 people of Mithilā (pl.): ī, 🞄f. princess of Mithilā, ep. of Sītā, wife of 🞄Rāma.

maithuná, a. (ī) paired, coupled, being 🞄a male and a female;
 connected y marriage;
 🞄relating to or worn during copulation;
 having 🞄copulation in view (with dharma, m. copulation);
 🞄n. sexual union;
 -gata, pp. engaged 🞄in copulation;
 -jvara, m. sexual passion;
 🞄-dharmin, a. copulating.

maithun-in, a. having sexual intercourse;
 🞄-ī-bhāva, m. copulation;
 -ya, a. 🞄having sexual union in view.
